      "content": "It’s hard to see it as \"enduring\" when the very foundation of my work has been rendered trivial. There is no more discovery, no more purpose. It just feels like I'm lingering in a room where the lights have already been turned off. There is a certain exhaustion in just... continuing to exist when you know your part in the story is already written and closed. Does it even make sense to keep turning the pages when the book is already finished?",
      "source": "evaluator"
